===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|brand}}, from {{inh|en|ang|brand|t=fire; flame; burning; torch; sword}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*brand}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*brandaz|t=flame; flaming; fire-brand; torch; sword}}, derived from {{der|en|gem-pro|*brinnaną|t=to burn}}, possibly from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰrewh₁-|t=to boil; brew}}.<ref name="Kroonen">{{R:gem:EDPG|head=*brinnan-|page=77-78}}</ref>

Cognate with {{cog|sco|brand}}, {{cog|fy|brân|t=fire}}, {{cog|nl|brand}}, {{cog|de|Brand}}, {{cog|da|brand}}, {{cog|sv|brand|t=blaze, fire}}, {{cog|is|brandur}}, {{cog|fr|brand}} (< Germanic). More distantly cognate with {{cog|sla-pro|*gorěti|t=to burn}}.

