===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[mark]] or [[scar]] made by burning with a hot iron, especially to mark [[cattle]] or to classify the contents of a [[cask]].
#: {{hypo|en|badge}}
#* {{RQ:Grey Light of Western Stars|page=59|passage=“Well, in the first place, every cattleman has to have a '''brand''' to identify his stock. Without it no cattleman, nor half a hundred cowboys, if he had so many, could ever recognize all the cattle in a big herd. {{...}}”}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=04 Dec 82|volume=10|number=20|journal=Gay Community News|page=9|author=Mitzel|title=A Sissy's Revenge|text=The indelible word "homosexual," like a '''brand''' that grew deeper and redder every day, became increasingly hard to conceal and to ignore.}}
# A [[branding iron]].
# The [[symbolic]] [[identity]], represented by a name and/or a logo, which indicates a certain product or service to the public.
#: {{syn|en|trademark|logo|brand name|marque|tradename|proprietary name}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Experiential marketing|page=39|author=Bernd Schmitt|year=1999|passage=The Amtrak '''brand''' revitalization approach represents one of the most ambitious, comprehensive, and systematic experiential marketing approaches I have ever seen.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Brandmindset|page=67|author=Duane E. Knapp|year=2000|passage=In this way, every Citibanker becomes a '''brand''' manager and an ambassador of the Citibank '''brand'''. ... Indeed, the Citibank '''brand''' will "never sleep"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Marshall Field's: The Store That Helped Build Chicago|page=136|author=Gayle Soucek|year=2010|passage=Mr. Lundgren claimed that Federated had conducted a focus group and the analysis showed that most people were either indifferent to the name change or preferred the Macy's '''brand'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|title=The attack of the MOOCs|url=http://www.economist.com/news/http://www.economist.com/news/business/21582001-army-new-online-courses-scaring-wits-out-traditional-universities-can-they|date=20 July 2013|volume=408|issue=8845|passage=Since the launch early last year of {{...}} two Silicon Valley start-ups offering free education through MOOCs, massive open online courses, the ivory towers of academia have been shaken to their foundations. University '''brands''' built in some cases over centuries have been forced to contemplate the possibility that information technology will rapidly make their existing business model obsolete.}}
# {{lb|en|business}} A specific [[product]], [[service]], or [[provider]] so distinguished.
#: {{ux|en|Some '''brands''' of breakfast cereal contain a lot of sugar.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Any specific [[type]] or [[variety]] of something; a distinct [[style]] or [[manner]].
#: {{ux|en|I didn’t appreciate his particular '''brand''' of flattery.}}
#: {{co|en|New Orleans '''brand''' sausage; Danish '''brand''' ham}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=w:Roger Cohen|title=The horror! The horror! The trauma of ISIS &#91;print version: ''International New York Times'', 18 November 2014, p.&nbsp;9&#93;|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/18/opinion/roger-cohen-the-evil-of-isis.html|date=17 November 2014|passage=[O]ne minute this "Jihadi John" was struggling to get by, and get accepted, in drizzly England, unemployed with a mortgage to pay and a chip on his shoulder, and the next he stands in brilliant Levantine sunlight, where everything is clear and etched, at the vanguard of some Sunni Risorgimento intent on subjecting the world to its murderous '''brand''' of Wahhabi Islam.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250716110448/https://www.nytimes.com/2014/11/18/opinion/roger-cohen-the-evil-of-isis.html|archivedate=16 July 2025}}
# The [[public]] [[image]] or [[reputation]] and [[recognized]], [[typical]] style of an [[individual]] or group.
#: {{syn|en|repute|name|good name}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Tom Bevan; Carl M. Cannon|title=Election 2012: The Battle Begins|publisher=Crown|isbn=9780307986627
|passage=The Obama '''brand''' had taken a hit two months earlier, when he campaigned for Creigh Deeds in Virginia and Jon Corzine in New Jersey, only to see them both lose.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|title=Start Your Own Personal Concierge Service|page=104|publisher=Entrepreneur Press|isbn=9781613081648
|passage=Her '''brand''' is edgy, cosmopolitan, and out-of-the-box, so blogging is the perfect, ever-changing match for her.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Sally Thorne|title=99 Percent Mine: A Novel|publisher=HarperCollins|isbn=9780062439628
|passage=He unplugged my umbilical cord to take a leisurely swig, smirking, watching me turn blue before giving it back. My cardiologist told me that was impossible, but I'm still convinced. That's very '''on-brand''' for [my twin] Jamie.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=David Segal|quotee=Simon Kuper|title=An Outsider Takes an Inside Look at the Oxford ‘Chums’ Who Run the U.K.|date=2022-05-14|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/14/books/simon-kuper-book-oxford.html|passage= “We made fun of [Jacob Rees-Mogg] in the paper” — that would be Cherwell, Oxford’s student-run weekly, where Kuper was a reporter — “all the while not realizing that we were helping to build his '''brand'''.”|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221014123736/https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/14/books/simon-kuper-book-oxford.html|archivedate=14 October 2022}}
