===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To burn the flesh with a hot iron, either as a marker (for criminals, slaves etc.) or to [[cauterise]] a wound.
#: {{ux|en|When they caught him, he was '''branded''' and then locked up.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1880|author=w:Richard Francis Burton|title=w:Os Lusíadas|volume=II|page=405|text=Man's flesh they eat: their own they paint and sear, / '''branding''' with burning iron, — usage fere!}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[mark#Verb|mark]] (especially cattle) with a [[#Noun|brand]] as [[proof]] of [[ownership]].
##: {{cot|en|earmark#Verb|chip<id:insert a microchip>}}
##: {{ux|en|The ranch hands had to '''brand''' every new calf by lunchtime.}}
##* {{RQ:Grey Light of Western Stars|page=59|passage=A maverick is an unbranded calf that has been weaned and shifts for itself. The maverick then belongs to the man who finds it and '''brands''' it.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make an indelible impression on the memory or senses.
#: {{ux|en|Her face is '''branded''' upon my memory.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[stigmatize]], [[label]] (someone).
#: {{ux|en|He was '''branded''' a fool by everyone that heard his story.}}
#* {{RQ:Ferguson Zollenstein|II
|passage=I had never defrauded a man of a farthing, nor called him knave behind his back. But now the last rag that covered my nakedness had been torn from me. I was '''branded''' a blackleg, card-sharper, and murderer.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=October 23, 2011|author=Phil McNulty| work=BBC Sport| title=Man Utd 1-6 Man City|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15325536.stm| passage=As Ferguson strode briskly towards the Stretford End at the final whistle, he will have been reflecting on the extent of the challenge now facing him from the club he once '''branded''' "noisy neighbours".}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|marketing}} To associate a product or service with a trademark or other name and related images.
#: {{ux|en|They '''branded''' the new detergent "Suds-O", with a nature scene inside a green O on the muted-colored recycled-cardboard box.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be [[very]] [[hot]], to [[burn]].
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|II||O, not for thee the glow, the bloom,<br>⁠Who changest not in any gale,<br>⁠Nor '''branding''' summer suns avail<br>To touch thy thousand years of gloom: […]}}

